r to seize control and playing the pair is the optimal move.\n\nReason: I have a pair of Kings and the Red Joker. With no 2s remaining, only a pair of Aces can beat my Kings. If the two missing Aces are split between the opponents, my Kings are invincible as a pair. Playing the Red Joker now secures the lead, allowing me to play the Kings next. If they clear, I play my last card (6) and win. Breaking the pair exposes my high cards to being beaten individually by the two missing Aces.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["RedJoker"]}'}
